    <Label Name="Label2" Style="17" DecimalsToShow="2" Text="Conic sections by five points" X="-8.12271630569667" Y="4.84187975225568" />
    <Label Name="Label3" Style="16" DecimalsToShow="2" Text="Let five points be given: A1, A2, A3, A4 and A5.\nWe can construct a conic section\npassing through these five points. To do\nthis, carry out the following:\n\n1. Draw line A2A3 and put point M on it.\n2. Draw lines A1A2, A3A4 and A4A5.\n3. Intersect A1A2 and A4A5 to obtain point M2.\n4. Intersect MM2 and A3A4 to obtain point M1.\n5. Draw lines MA5 and A1M1.\n6. Locate point A at the intersection of these lines.\n7. Make A leave trace and slide M along A2A3. \n\nHow does this work?" X="-7.91104943128111" Y="3.88937881738571" />
  </Figures>
